{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"24c19653-2b68-4b34-9b88-ab0072c097de","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\"findings\":[{\"area\":\"framing_and_limits\",\"detail\":\"The input size limit is enforced by reading up to MAX_BYTES + 1 (131073 bytes) and checking length before decoding UTF-8. Empty input returns an empty string without raising an error.\",\"severity\":\"info\"},{\"area\":\"json_and_validation\",\"detail\":\"Validation uses object_pairs_hook=unique_object and parse_constant=reject_constant with json.loads, strictly rejecting duplicate keys and nonfinite numeric constants. Strict type checks and regex validation ensure graph node and edge compliance.\",\"severity\":\"info\"},{\"area\":\"topological_algorithms\",\"detail\":\"Topological ordering uses a min-heap over in-degree 0 nodes, ensuring lexicographically smallest available node selection. Layers are computed in independent sorted rounds from copied in-degrees without mutating graph structures.\",\"severity\":\"info\"},{\"area\":\"error_handling_and_atomicity\",\"detail\":\"Whole-batch processing buffers and validates all requests before writing to stdout. Any validation or parsing failure directs stderr output exactly to 'topo-plan: invalid input\\\\n' and exits with status 2.\",\"severity\":\"info\"}],\"reason\":\"The implementation in topo_plan.py, along with README.md and criteria.md, strictly adheres to the functional contract, correctly handles NDJSON batch atomicity, edge limits, duplicate edge consolidation, and lexicographic topological ordering versus layered rounds.\",\"schema\":1,\"tests_executed\":false,\"verdict\":\"accept\"}\n","duration_seconds":94.957557581,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":25380,"output_tokens":11473,"thinking_tokens":11190,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":36853}}}
